notes.content:
Import scheme: package. Run: python main.py. Smoke: echo quit | python main.py. Files: src/models.py, src/constants.py, src/loader.py, src/parser.py, src/combat.py, src/save_load.py, src/engine.py, main.py.
Data shapes:
  world.yaml → src.loader.py: mapping with keys rooms, items, npcs, monsters, player_start
State contracts:
  GameState (owner src.models.GameState, consumers src.engine, src.save_load): {
  "player": {
    "location": "room_id",
    "health": int,
    "max_health": int,
    "attack": int,
    "defense": int,
    "inventory": ["item_id", ...],
    "equipped": {"weapon": "item_id|null", "armor": "item_id|null"}
  },
  "rooms": {
    "room_id": {
      "items": ["item_id", ...],
      "npcs": ["npc_id", ...],
      "monster": "monster_id|null",
      "visited": bool
    },
    ...
  },
  "npcs": {
    "npc_id": {"dialogue_index": int},
    ...
  },
  "monsters": {
    "monster_id": {"defeated": bool},
    ...
  }
}
  Save file JSON (owner src.save_load, consumers src.save_load, src.engine): Exactly the same schema as GameState (see above) serialized to a single JSON object.

Root cause: {"choice": "trace", "symbolref": "src/constants.py:init__"}
Recommended fix: {"choice": "trace", "symbolref": "src/constants.py:init__"}
Target: src/combat.py

